<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Iarmumu</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 850 CE (approx.) · capital Killarney</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The early medieval kingdom of West Munster around Killarney's lakes, ruled by the Eoganacht Locha Lein, rivals of the Munster kings at Cashel.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Iarmumu took shape in south-west Ireland by the 6th century, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eoganacht</a> Locha Lein, a branch of the dynasties ruling <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a>, established themselves around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-leane">Loch Lein</a>, the Lower Lake at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/killarney">Killarney</a>. Their territory covered much of later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ciarraige-luachra">Kerry</a> and west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-cork">Cork</a>, and they ruled over earlier peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corcu-duibne">Corcu Duibne</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings of Iarmumu sometimes claimed the kingship of all <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a>, but were usually excluded from the rotation of Cashel's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eoganacht</a> branches. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inisfallen">Inisfallen</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-leane">Loch Lein</a> became an important monastery, later home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-inisfallen">Annals of Inisfallen</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">Cattle</a> wealth and client peoples supported the dynasty.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The dynasty declined from the 8th century, and in the 11th and 12th centuries the Ui Donnchada, a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganacht-raithlind">Eoganacht Raithlind</a> driven west from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-cork">Cork</a>, took over the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-leane">Loch Lein</a>. The area then fell within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-desmond">Kingdom of Desmond</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthys</a>, with the O'Donoghues as local lords around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/killarney">Killarney</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 500 CE – 850 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:69.65%;width:6.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 850 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Killarney</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>West Munster, Eoganacht Locha Lein</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=kingdom-of-iarmumu" aria-label="Kingdom of Iarmumu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4466 379 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Iarmumu lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4786 635L4823 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4823 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4786 635h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4786 635h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Killarney. <a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=kingdom-of-iarmumu">On the atlas 